# Blocks use Cubix components only

Every sample, block template (`components/blocks/templates/**`), and docs example must be composed **only** from components in `components/cubix/*` (imported as `@/components/cubix/<name>`). This applies to both the live view and the copyable source string.

## Use the component, not a hand-made copy

- Interactive UI: `Button`, `InputGroup*`, `Input`, `Field`, `Select`, `Tabs`, `Badge`, `Card*`, `Empty*`, `Separator`, `Kbd`, `Tooltip`, `Sheet`, `Drawer`, `Dialog`, `ScrollArea`, `Skeleton`, `Avatar`, `Table`, agent components (`Conversation`, `PromptInput`, `Message`, ...).
- Never ship a raw `<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>`, hand-rolled card/badge/divider/overlay, or a custom drawer when a Cubix component exists.
- Semantic wrappers with no Cubix equivalent are fine: `<nav>`, `<ul>/<li>`, `<dl>`, `<form>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`, `<main>`, `<img>`, text `<p>/<span>/<h1>`.

## Style through the system, not around it

- Use the component's own `variant` / `size` props first.
- Do not re-skin a component with className color overrides (e.g. `bg-foreground text-background` on `Button`). If a needed look is missing, add it as a real `cva` variant in all three bases (Base UI, React Aria, Radix) and its docs, then use that variant.
- Layout/spacing classes on components (`mt-*`, `w-full`, `min-w-*`, `gap-*`) are fine.
- Typography only from Typeset tokens: `text-display`, `text-headline`, `text-title`, `text-lead`, `text-body`, `text-description`, `text-caption`, `text-label`.
- Colors only from tokens; no hex/rgb.

## Persian text

- No `font-mono` and no `tracking-*` on Persian strings (breaks letter joining). Keep those for Latin labels like `Error 404`.

```tsx
// BAD
<button className="rounded-lg bg-primary px-4 py-2">بازگشت</button>
<Button className="bg-foreground text-background">بازگشت</Button>

// GOOD
<Button render={<Link href="/" />} nativeButton={false}>بازگشت</Button>
<Button variant="outline">مستندات</Button>
```
